Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Custom Back Button + Navigation Interception

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();

        // Custom back button text
        Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
        {
            TextOverride = "Cancel",
            Command = new Command(async () => await TryNavigateBack())
        });
    }

    // Intercept hardware/gesture back navigation
    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the async dialog; return true to cancel navigation
            MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () => await TryNavigateBack());
            return true; // Cancel default back behavior
        }

        return false; // Allow normal navigation
    }

    private async Task TryNavigateBack()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave)
                return; // User chose to stay
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }

    // Call this whenever form data changes
    private void OnFormFieldChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
        _hasUnsavedChanges = true;
    }
}
```

## Key Points

| Mechanism | What it handles |
|-----------|----------------|
| `BackButtonBehavior.Command` | Shell toolbar back button (shows "Cancel") |
| `OnBackButtonPressed()` | Android hardware back, swipe gestures |

## Caveats

- **iOS swipe-back gesture**: `OnBackButtonPressed` doesn't fire for the iOS edge-swipe. To fully block it, disable the gesture via a platform-specific handler or set `Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior` with `IsEnabled = false` while changes are unsaved, then re-enable on save.
- Always navigate with `Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..")` rather than popping the navigation stack directly, so Shell routing stays consistent.
